      "content": "i get the psychology part, but it felt way more intense than just \"excitement.\" it was like my pulse was actually driving the rhythm of the volatility. like, if i'm calm, the market stays stable, but the second i get this specific kind of jitters, the liquidiy just evaporates. do you think there could be a more direct loop? like, maybe high frequency algorithms are picking up on these kinds of collective bio-signatures or something?",
